]:mb-4\n      [&amp;_h6]:text-sm md:[&amp;_h6]:text-base [&amp;_h6]:font-medium [&amp;_h6]:mb-4\n      [&amp;_p]:text-base md:[&amp;_p]:text-lg [&amp;_p]:mb-3 [&amp;_p]:opacity-70\n      [&amp;_blockquote]:pl-4 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-l-4 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-gray-300  [&amp;_blockquote]:italic [&amp;_blockquote]:my-4\n      [&amp;_table]:w-full\n      [&amp;_table]:border\n      [&amp;_table]:border-collapse\n      [&amp;_table]:mb-6\n      [&amp;_th]:text-left [&amp;_th]:border [&amp;_th]:px-4 [&amp;_th]:py-2\n      [&amp;_td]:border [&amp;_td]:px-4 [&amp;_td]:py-2\n      [&amp;_li]:mb-2\n      [&amp;_section]:mb-6\n    \"><p>helo</p><h2><strong>Onitsuka Tiger Mexico 66 | White/Blue/Red Tricolor (Men's 7A First Copy)</strong></h2><h3><strong>The Definitive Heritage Masterpiece</strong></h3><p>The <strong>Onitsuka Tiger Mexico 66</strong> in \"White/Blue/Red\" is the most famous colorway in the brand?s history, originally debuted during the 1966 Olympic pre-trials. This <strong>7A Master Quality (First Copy)</strong> replica for men captures the essential \"Tricolor\" spirit, combining a clean white leather base with the signature blue and red Tiger stripes. It is the gold standard for retro sneakers, offering a slim, sophisticated profile that has remained a global fashion staple for over 60 years.</p><h3><strong>Key Features</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>7A Master Quality Build:</strong> A top-tier 1:1 replica that meticulously recreates the signature low-profile racing last and the lightweight, \"barefoot\" feel of the 1960s original.</li><li><strong>The Iconic Tricolor Palette:</strong> Features a crisp <strong>White</strong> (or slightly off-white Birch) leather upper accented by vibrant <strong>Direct Blue and Fiery Red</strong> stripes, providing a timeless, sporty aesthetic.</li><li><strong>Premium Leather Construction:</strong> Crafted with soft, fine-grain leather and reinforced with <strong>light grey or tan suede</strong> overlays on the T-toe and heel-cross for structural durability.</li><li><strong>Heritage Design Details:</strong> Includes the classic \"Tiger\" branded heel flap and the cross-stitched heel reinforcement designed for better stability and that authentic '66 look.</li><li><strong>OrthoLite-Style Cushioning:</strong> Equipped with a moisture-managing, cushioned footbed to provide modern comfort and impact protection for all-day urban wear.</li><li><strong>Thin Traction Outsole:</strong> Features a flexible, low-profile rubber outsole with the traditional herringbone tread pattern for a grounded feel and reliable grip.</li></ul><h3><strong>Product Specifications</strong></h3><figure class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><strong>Feature</strong></th><th><strong>Details</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Quality Grade</strong></td><td>7A / Master Copy (Heritage Tier)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Price Range</strong></td><td><strong>Rs. 3,600</strong> (Current 2026 market price in India)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sizes Available</strong></td><td>Euro 41 to 45 (UK 7 to 11 / Men's)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Primary Materials</strong></td><td>Leather / Suede / Rubber Outsole</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Packaging</strong></td><td>Includes Onitsuka Tiger brand-accurate box and tags</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h3><strong>Shipping &amp; Delivery (India)</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Express Dispatch:</strong> Orders are usually processed and shipped within <strong>24 hours</strong> from Indian hubs (Surat, Delhi, Mumbai).</li><li><strong>Estimated Timeline:</strong> 3?5 working days for metro cities; 5?7 days for other regions via <strong>BlueDart or Delhivery</strong>.</li><li><strong>Payment Options:</strong><ul><li><strong>Cash on Delivery (COD):</strong> Available. Most premium sellers require a small advance \"security\" fee (<strong>Rs. 200 to Rs. 500</strong>) to confirm the order.</li><li><strong>Prepaid Benefits:</strong> Often includes <strong>free shipping</strong> or a 10% discount for payments via UPI/Google Pay.</li></ul></li></ul><h3><strong>Sizing &amp; Care Tip</strong></h3><blockquote><p><strong>Fit Note:</strong> The Mexico 66 has a <strong>notoriously narrow, streamlined fit</strong>. For men with standard or narrow feet, stay true to your Euro size. If you have <strong>wider feet</strong>, it is highly recommended to <strong>order one full size up</strong> (e.g., if you wear UK 8, order UK 9) to ensure comfort across the midfoot. To clean, wipe the white leather with a damp cloth and use a specific suede brush for the toe overlays; avoid using wet wipes on the colored stripes to prevent any potential color transfer.</p></blockquote></div>","productDescription":null,"productBrand":"Onitsuk_a Tiger","sizeName":"[]","catName":"Men's Shoes","availability":"true"}]
