p;_h6]:font-medium [&amp;_h6]:mb-4\n      [&amp;_p]:text-base md:[&amp;_p]:text-lg [&amp;_p]:mb-3 [&amp;_p]:opacity-70\n      [&amp;_blockquote]:pl-4 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-l-4 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-gray-300  [&amp;_blockquote]:italic [&amp;_blockquote]:my-4\n      [&amp;_table]:w-full\n      [&amp;_table]:border\n      [&amp;_table]:border-collapse\n      [&amp;_table]:mb-6\n      [&amp;_th]:text-left [&amp;_th]:border [&amp;_th]:px-4 [&amp;_th]:py-2\n      [&amp;_td]:border [&amp;_td]:px-4 [&amp;_td]:py-2\n      [&amp;_li]:mb-2\n      [&amp;_section]:mb-6\n    \"><h2><i><strong>Onitsuka Tiger Mexico Delegation | Pine Green/Cream</strong></i></h2><h3><strong>The 1968 Olympic Heritage Revival</strong></h3><p>Step into Olympic history with the <strong>Mexico Delegation</strong>. While the Mexico 66 is the brand's most famous silhouette, the <strong>Delegation</strong> is the actual faithful reproduction of the footwear worn by the Japanese Delegation during the <strong>1968 Mexico City Olympic Parade of Nations</strong>. In this vibrant \"Pine Green/Cream\" colorway, the shoe offers a rich, forest-inspired aesthetic that perfectly captures the \"varsity\" spirit of the late 1960s.</p><h3><strong>Key Features</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Authentic 1968 Design:</strong> A meticulous reinterpretation of the original parade shoe, preserving the structural details and vintage athletic spirit of the 1960s Japanese national team.</li><li><strong>Premium Suede Construction:</strong> Features a high-quality <strong>Pine Green</strong> suede upper that provides a soft, comfortable fit and a textured, premium feel compared to smooth leather models.</li><li><strong>Iconic \"MEXICO\" Branding:</strong> Distinguished by the bold \"MEXICO\" mark emblazoned on the side?a unique identifier specific to the Delegation model.</li><li><strong>Track-Inspired Details:</strong> Includes a unique sockliner graphic inspired by an <strong>athletics track</strong>, paying homage to the shoe's track and field roots.</li><li><strong>Modern Comfort Engineering:</strong> Equipped with Onitsuka Tiger's proprietary soft insoles that provide firm heel support and all-day comfort for urban use.</li><li><strong>Lightweight Sole:</strong> S sits on a supple, elastomer/rubber outsole that offers reliable traction while maintaining a lightweight, low-profile feel.</li></ul><h3><strong>History &amp; Craftsmanship</strong></h3><p>The Mexico Delegation was launched to celebrate the 50th anniversary of the 1968 games, ensuring that the original structure and production methods were maintained as closely as possible. The \"Pine Green/Cream\" edition is particularly noted for its <strong>serrated suede details</strong> and creamy off-white stripes, which evoke a classic retro-tennis or training shoe aesthetic.</p><h3><strong>Sizing &amp; Care</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Unisex Fit:</strong> Listed in US Men's/Unisex sizing. Women are generally advised to refer to the size guide and select <strong>1.5 sizes down</strong> from their standard Women's size (e.g., a Men's 7 is a Women's 8.5).</li><li><strong>Narrow Profile:</strong> Like most heritage Onitsuka Tigers, these run slightly narrow. Those with wider feet may consider going <strong>up a half size</strong> for additional comfort.</li><li><strong>Maintenance:</strong> Because it is crafted from natural suede, it is recommended to clean with a soft brush and avoid heavy water exposure to prevent color transfer.</li></ul></div>","productDescription":null,"productBrand":"Onitsuk_a Tiger","sizeName":"[]","catName":"Men's Shoes","availability":0}]
